    },
    {
      "ordinal": 29,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "5.2",
      "title": "Chest",
      "body": "The torso and the back must be protected with metal plates.\n\nChainmail elements can be used as an additional protection or as an articulation of plate elements.\n\nAn under-armor layer protecting the torso and the back is mandatory, commonly called gambeson. It should consist of at least a layer of felted fabric quilted with fabric.\n\nIt is allowed and recommended to wear concealed modern protection for the back.\n\nHips protection is mandatory. If the torso protection is not long enough to cover the hips in standing position, competitors can use a metal scale skirt, hidden metal plates attached to gambeson, or other permitted protection displayed in Authenticity Rule documents.",
      "page_from": 8,
      "page_to": 8,
      "stable_key": "armor-requirements:5.2",
      "parent_key": "armor-requirements:5",
      "review_status": "extracted",
